    {"path": "MathlibExt/AlgebraicTopology/ModelCategory/DerivedMapping/Basic.lean", "backport": "not-needed", "disposition": "diverged", "published_sha256": "1a5708c65a2f524a0c904664e43e8537ec87c0066c95fad797078ce919628550", "rationale": "Expose how both variance maps are computed on actual replacement arrows by Mathlib's enriched whiskering operations, and prove the mixed square directly by naturality of the bifunctor.", "upstream_commit": "efb0b86f464b1cd2243085ad50810fd0ac3c0d07", "upstream_sha256": "856258effb76e85ec899c0dc440b36b48144f580fba23502dfab68091e0b8aee"},
    {"path": "MathlibExt/AlgebraicTopology/ModelCategory/HomotopyCategory.lean", "backport": "not-needed", "disposition": "diverged", "published_sha256": "d142882833bc6dd9477733e7a725d86386e7d1e9ae66a83339c9665420a03150", "rationale": "Keep the general localization detection theorem. Prove its fibration case using Mathlib's FundamentalLemma and a covering homotopy to obtain a strict section, then use weak-equivalence stability under retracts. Use Mathlib's localization and quotient APIs directly instead of publishing aliases and convenience wrappers.", "upstream_commit": "efb0b86f464b1cd2243085ad50810fd0ac3c0d07", "upstream_sha256": "f022081a994922cf181f3b94452574459361480cee070f7e423902f0b3281626"},
    {"path": "MathlibExt/AlgebraicTopology/ModelCategory/QuillenAdjunction.lean", "backport": "not-needed", "disposition": "diverged", "published_sha256": "133ceeccb7d8037c6e12cbc62a50b205d137024f31b3f5c9bfb21bac6aa0d5df", "rationale": "Use the pinned Mathlib's initial- and terminal-object preservation lemmas in the Quillen object-preservation proofs instead of rebuilding uniqueness of maps from the adjunction. Retain the Atlas header and add API documentation and original source credit.", "upstream_commit": "efb0b86f464b1cd2243085ad50810fd0ac3c0d07", "upstream_sha256": "5d00e88d0e17fc592ef2a5a821314eac04b6ea9c40453bdcbc0e0e81b144beea"},
    {"path": "MathlibExt/AlgebraicTopology/ModelCategory/QuillenBrown.lean", "backport": "not-needed", "disposition": "diverged", "published_sha256": "babf0c790805713eb9b3e658761419c00ce8926c1eac0ee33806371ebccbb22a", "rationale": "Use the pinned Mathlib cofibrant Brown factorization and recover fibrant Brown preservation by applying the first theorem to the opposite Quillen adjunction, instead of maintaining a separate fibrant factorization proof.", "upstream_commit": "efb0b86f464b1cd2243085ad50810fd0ac3c0d07", "upstream_sha256": "572ffe5c869b6205ab6b09db24a821b504e2f5355bd1761050d6064153e3f217"},
    {"path": "MathlibExt/AlgebraicTopology/ModelCategory/QuillenEquivalence.lean", "backport": "not-needed", "disposition": "diverged", "published_sha256": "567710fa75b9cf5d7d5a74aefcd92e04cccfe8921a9029da1c284acdde9a1de8", "rationale": "Use the actual target object as the explicit Hovey-criterion endpoint in the counit proof, rather than adding a fibrancy instance for its image under the identity functor. Retain the Atlas header, place the mathematical overview after imports, and credit the original source authors.", "upstream_commit": "efb0b86f464b1cd2243085ad50810fd0ac3c0d07", "upstream_sha256": "e5cd2e9792b9bec7228b1cf0375381268d5c3aff06e65586db9d0c6f1d7564c6"},
    {"path": "MathlibExt/AlgebraicTopology/ModelCategory/QuillenEquivalenceCancellation.lean", "backport": "not-needed", "disposition": "diverged", "published_sha256": "14ff42342083beba7fb3ffcda6f823b06354f79591885158faf8631322cd906f", "rationale": "Import Brown explicitly rather than relying on the recognition module to export it. Use the inverse hom-equivalence to discharge the replacement-map weak equivalence and apply Mathlib's precomposition equivalences directly to both sides of the original adjoint-map criterion.", "upstream_commit": "efb0b86f464b1cd2243085ad50810fd0ac3c0d07", "upstream_sha256": "53136bf667902c6fa2ff60ca2e5e9654beb6dd022bd0420a7a1abd526bc0b63b"},
    {"path": "MathlibExt/AlgebraicTopology/ModelCategory/QuillenEquivalenceCriterion.lean", "backport": "not-needed", "disposition": "diverged", "published_sha256": "454a00d36ff2d3701d989bfd42d51777e4475a4353f424c08faea0ef160a99ab", "rationale": "Remove the unused Brown import. Apply Mathlib's weak-factorization-system lifting lemma directly to the mapped trivial cofibration, and carry the endpoint hypotheses through the two precomposition equivalences.", "upstream_commit": "efb0b86f464b1cd2243085ad50810fd0ac3c0d07", "upstream_sha256": "1d6d9dc9f683d716a04507cf1f37558550d344170d09b76944cffc90e0bbafae"},
    {"path": "MathlibExt/AlgebraicTopology/ModelCategory/QuillenEquivalenceRightCancellation.lean", "backport": "not-needed", "disposition": "diverged", "published_sha256": "3dcaf31291d714a28270ad91bb9917451d24aff1181558bdb2a921cbaf350bf2", "rationale": "Use the pinned Mathlib weak-factorization-system lift on the original replacement square, then pass directly through the adjoint-map criteria for the second adjunction and the composite, using Mathlib's postcomposition equivalences to eliminate the replacement maps.", "upstream_commit": "efb0b86f464b1cd2243085ad50810fd0ac3c0d07", "upstream_sha256": "cc605f1f78bba93015d0c22772dafb20c2aa3a6909510762ca79f551218d39c5"},
    {"path": "MathlibExt/AlgebraicTopology/ModelCategory/QuillenFibrantCriterion.lean", "backport": "not-needed", "disposition": "diverged", "published_sha256": "f5675445ea9fe6ac290dff3f5b978bea19e0d9330a476180be21e0c6babf1533", "rationale": "Use Mathlib's fibrant resolution and canonical localization directly, with the general saturation theorem for weak equivalences. Detect invertibility via the split-epimorphic monomorphism furnished by the lift. Include both directions of the Joyal–Tierney criterion and omit duplicate accessors and Brown wrappers.", "upstream_commit": "efb0b86f464b1cd2243085ad50810fd0ac3c0d07", "upstream_sha256": "1f2be3b4966e1c2c29cdd162360d3b8e9a97862fa482d98f0859302ea9712cf6"},
